Season 63, Episode 1: Standing Again

Cold Open — Plateau Shelter
Late morning. Sunlight slants across the reed mats. Sam pushes himself up on his elbows, wobbling but determined. Kellyn moves to steady him, but he waves them back with a faint smile.

Sam (hoarse but resolute):
“I need to feel the ground under me. If I can’t stand, I can’t remember.”

Title Card: Standing Again

⸻

Act I — The First Step
With Alex bracing his arm, Sam slowly rises. His knees buckle once, but Peter slides behind, catching him. Sam exhales, sweat beading on his brow.

Peter (dry, half-teasing):
“You weigh less than Estrella, but you fall harder.”
Sam (grinning faintly):
“Good. Means I still have gravity.”

Jonathan chuckles, tension breaking as Sam straightens, trembling but upright.

⸻

Act II — The Trial of Balance
They walk him outside. Estrella flicks her ears as Sam takes his first uneven steps across the plateau dust. The sheep shuffle close, steadying the rhythm of the group.

Sam (breathing hard):
“I dreamed of this. Of walking with you. But in the dream, the ground sang back.”

Jonathan hums low, testing the resonance against the wind. Alex narrows his eyes, listening. Kellyn steadies Sam’s shoulder, not pressing, just holding space.

⸻

Act III — The Memory Returns
Later, seated on a flat rock, Sam closes his eyes. His voice is clearer than before.

Sam:
“The loci… they’re not just machines. They’re listeners. They take the shape of whoever approaches. That’s why my memories fracture — they weren’t all mine. Some were reflections. Echoes.”

Kellyn frowns, leaning in.
Kellyn (quiet, sharp):
“So they mirrored you back at yourself. And you thought it was prophecy.”

Sam nods, eyes wet.
Sam:
“And sometimes, it still feels true.”

⸻

Act IV — The Covenant of Return
Back in the shelter, Sam lowers himself carefully onto his mat. This time, he does it without help.

Sam (firm, steady):
“I’m not healed. But I’m not gone, either. I’ll walk with you again. Not today. But soon.”

Kellyn presses the damp cloth into his hand.
Kellyn (softly):
“Then start here. Care for yourself the way we’ve cared for you. That’s covenant too.”

Sam nods, clutching the cloth, and for the first time, he doesn’t look like he’s fading — he looks like he’s returning.

⸻

Closing Image
Sam sitting upright on his mat, cloth in hand, light pooling around him. The others watch from a distance — wary, relieved, uncertain. For the first time, the balance of strength begins to shift again.

Narration (Kellyn’s voice):
“He stood, and the weight shifted. Not fully, not clean. But enough to remind us: even those pulled under can return. And return changes everything.”

Fade out.
End of Episode 1.  

